1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,134
Tomi compares historical Encyclopaedia Britannica with Wikipedia, making evidence and uncertainty visible.

2
00:00:06,134 --> 00:00:15,847
This demonstration shows the real NVIDIA pipeline, three narrowly supported comparisons, and three clear failures from our own runs.

3
00:00:15,847 --> 00:00:23,428
We selected one hundred pages from a pinned dataset, using random sampling without replacement and a recorded seed.

4
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:29,746
Every image has a checked hash and a real Nemotron Parse three point five receipt.

5
00:00:29,746 --> 00:00:37,327
The sample contains ninety-five full text pages, one partial astronomy plate, three blank leaves, and one non-text cover.

6
00:00:37,327 --> 00:00:40,697
These are extraction outcomes, not certified OCR accuracy.

7
00:00:40,697 --> 00:00:43,113
Parse extracts the historical documents.

8
00:00:43,113 --> 00:00:46,979
Wikipedia candidates come from the organizer’s versioned snapshot.

9
00:00:46,979 --> 00:00:52,295
Nemotron Embed and Rerank run together on our assigned Nebius GPU.

10
00:00:52,295 --> 00:00:55,678
LanceDB stores vectors in Azure Blob storage.

11
00:00:55,678 --> 00:01:01,477
Nemotron Super VL, accessed through Token Factory, drives the Hermes comparison agent.

12
00:01:01,477 --> 00:01:04,377
Credentials stay behind the Rust gateway.

13
00:01:04,377 --> 00:01:06,817
Here are the three supported cases.

14
00:01:06,817 --> 00:01:11,291
Shipbuilding contrasts timber shelf-pieces with the modern definition of a shipyard.

15
00:01:11,291 --> 00:01:15,358
Both measurement excerpts associate the litre with a cubic decimetre.

16
00:01:15,358 --> 00:01:21,459
Bleaching compares historical attention to vessels and gas with the modern purpose of removing colour.

17
00:01:21,459 --> 00:01:24,713
We reviewed these limited claims against their sources.

18
00:01:24,713 --> 00:01:27,153
Independent human sign-off is still pending.

19
00:01:27,153 --> 00:01:29,008
The broader questions failed.

20
00:01:29,008 --> 00:01:30,864
Shipbuilding retrieval favored companies.

21
00:01:30,864 --> 00:01:34,574
Measurement retrieval found policy instead of unit definitions.

22
00:01:34,574 --> 00:01:39,212
Damaged bleaching text could not support a full process comparison.

23
00:01:39,212 --> 00:01:42,923
We preserve those original attempts and their abstentions.

24
00:01:42,923 --> 00:01:48,953
Later narrow successes do not erase the failed questions or establish general accuracy.

25
00:01:48,953 --> 00:01:53,714
Our Hermes extension gives the model immutable evidence span identifiers.

26
00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:58,950
The server resolves selected identifiers into exact quotes and Unicode offsets.

27
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:04,663
Unknown identifiers, changed quotations, and references from only one corpus fail validation.

28
00:02:04,663 --> 00:02:10,852
This repairs quotation-copy errors while leaving factual entailment as a separate review step.

29
00:02:10,852 --> 00:02:21,942
The static archive includes all hundred scans, editable LaTeX, individual PDFs, and a compiled hundred-document volume totaling one hundred eighty-seven pages.

30
00:02:21,942 --> 00:02:26,167
The matching ledger records candidates, ambiguity and blockers.

31
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:29,864
Relevance scores are not probabilities of truth.

32
00:02:29,864 --> 00:02:35,144
Original source revisions, hashes, comparison metrics and failures remain inspectable.

33
00:02:35,144 --> 00:02:42,288
The application connects streaming chat, source cards, the evidence canvas and a three-dimensional graph.

34
00:02:42,288 --> 00:02:44,839
Stored conversation evidence survives reload.

35
00:02:44,839 --> 00:02:51,472
The repository contains setup instructions, sample selection, comparison analysis and six documented cases.

36
00:02:51,472 --> 00:02:58,104
The result is an inspectable research workflow with useful answers and visible limits.
